PYTHON LAB 4 - READ THE ONBOARD TEMPERATURE DEVICE

Create /tmp/temp.py:

  fd = open("/dev/adc/temp", 0)
  if fd < 0:
      print("sensor unavailable")
  else:
      data = read(fd, 32)
      print(data)
      close(fd)

Run: python /tmp/temp.py
Expected: a byte-list containing the device's textual output,
which depends on hardware and environment. Do not assume a fixed C.

Alternative MCP tool: get_temperature() returns a sensor reading
without starting a child interpreter. The script teaches the file
API and the device node. For more precise sensor semantics inspect
help adc or /man/adc-workflow. Never assume standard Python APIs.
